A||||2||Smokin87||Tire rotation||||1||
Z||000000||Smokin87||01-17-2001||03:15 PM||||i want to rotate the tires on my stock 87 GT.  but i dont know if the front tires are smaller than the back.  does anyone know the procedure to rotate tires.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||01-17-2001||04:25 PM||||Just read the tire size on the sidewall of your tires.  The front were originally 205/60-15 while the rears were 215/60-15.  On both of my 87 GT's I recently purchased had 215/60-15's all around.  <P>If the tire sizes are different, you should only swap side to side, keeping the front tires on the front and rears to the rear.  If they are all the same size, you can cross them.  This is spelled out in the original owners manual if you still have one with the car.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||01-18-2001||09:15 AM||||Be careful that you do not have directional tires.  Some tires are only designed to rotate in one direction.  If you have that kind  and have different sizes front and back then you can only allign the car regularly because you can not switch from side to side.||||reg||1
